/F2 12 Tf 72 700 Td (Abstract) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 72 683 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 666 Td (We construct, in Cubical Agda, a sheaf-level linear--nonlinear adjunction over a finite) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 653 Td (point-generated actor-causal site. The site is restricted to supported finite frames: every) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 640 Td (actor appearing in a frame is incident to some event. Its topology is generated by the) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 627 Td (canonical cover of a frame by its single-event point subframes. For any value category with) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 614 Td (finite products, the resulting pointification functor sends a presheaf to the product of its) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 601 Td (event-local values; this functor is proved to be left adjoint to the inclusion of point) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 588 Td (sheaves into supported presheaves. Given a value-level Benton linear--nonlinear adjunction) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 575 Td (and finite products on the linear value category, this reflector removes the sheafification) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 562 Td (hypothesis from the point-generated sheaf bridge and yields a machine-checked adjunction) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 549 Td (between cartesian-valued and linear-valued point sheaves.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 536 Td () Tj
/F2 12 Tf 72 523 Td (The mathematical statement) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 72 506 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 489 Td (Let A be an actor base, and let SFin_A be the category of supported finite actor-causal) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 476 Td (frames. Objects are finite local frames whose actors are all supported by events; morphisms) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 463 Td (are the strict frame embeddings used by the actor-causal site, restricted to supported) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 450 Td (frames. The point topology on SFin_A is generated by the canonical family {pt_e\(F\) -> F}_{e) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 437 Td (in E\(F\)}, where pt_e\(F\) is the one-event subframe incident at e. This is deliberately the) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 424 Td (event-discrete topology: it records the universal reconstruction of a frame from its event-) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 411 Td (local views, while leaving causal and higher-overlap refinements for later topologies.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 398 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 385 Td (For a category C with finite products, write PSh_A\(C\) = [SFin_A^op, C] for the implemented) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 372 Td (category of supported presheaves, and let PtSh_A\(C\) be the full subcategory of point) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 359 Td (sheaves. The point sheaf condition is the descent condition for the canonical point cover;) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 346 Td (equivalently, a presheaf is determined by its event-local values. The formalization proves) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 333 Td (this equivalence as a comparison between point descent and a product-locality condition.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 320 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 307 Td (The reflector is explicit: a_C\(P\)\(F\) = product_{e in E\(F\)} P\(pt_e\(F\)\). Restrictions are) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 294 Td (induced by the corresponding point-to-point morphisms. The proof that this is functorial,) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 281 Td (point-local, and universal is carried out behind an abstract finite-product interface, so) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 268 Td (that Agda does not unfold products into enumeration-dependent normal forms during) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 255 Td (unification. The machine-checked result is an adjunction a_C |- iota_C, where iota_C:) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 242 Td (PtSh_A\(C\) -> PSh_A\(C\) is the inclusion.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 229 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 216 Td (Now suppose Cart is a cartesian value category with finite products, V is the category) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 203 Td (underlying a star-autonomous value structure and also has finite products, and F |- G : Cart) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 190 Td (<-> V is a Benton-style value-level adjunction. Postcomposition lifts F and G to supported) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 177 Td (presheaf categories, with a pointwise adjunction F_* |- G_*. The right adjoint preserves) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 164 Td (point sheaves: descent along the point cover is transported across the natural bijection) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 151 Td (Cart\(X,GY\) ~= V\(FX,Y\). The left adjoint is made sheaf-level by reflection. Thus R_pt = G_*) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 138 Td (restricted to PtSh_A\(V\), and L_pt = a_V F_* iota_Cart.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 125 Td () Tj
