/F2 12 Tf 72 669 Td (Scope and significance) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 72 652 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 635 Td (The theorem is modest but precise. It is a Grothendieck-style descent result over a finite) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 622 Td (site, a Lawvere-style use of adjointness as structure, and a Benton-style linear--nonlinear) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 609 Td (bridge lifted from values to sheaves. The point-generated topology is intentionally small:) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 596 Td (it proves that event-local observations freely generate a coherent sheaf-level object and) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 583 Td (that this reconstruction is compatible with a linear--nonlinear value adjunction.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 570 Td () Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 557 Td (Equally important are the limitations. The theorem does not construct the value-level) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 544 Td (adjunction F |- G; it assumes it. It does not yet instantiate the linear value category with) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 531 Td (a concrete sessions model satisfying the finite-products hypothesis. It is not a full) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 518 Td (sheafification theorem for all finite actor-causal covers, nor a comparison with a Cubical) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 505 Td (library coverage for the point topology. Finally, it is not the cross-site adjunction to the) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 492 Td (modal side. It is the first checked bridge on the operational side: point-generated) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 72 479 Td (sheafification plus a sheaf-level linear--nonlinear adjunction.) Tj
